{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_014aQWvc5iszNegmFGAibZiD","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t\"\"\"attavo: the command.\n2\t\n3\t    attavo doctor [TENANT_ROOT] [--json]\n4\t    attavo spec-gate [N]\n5\t    attavo approve [N] --by LOGIN\n6\t    attavo approval-status [N]\n7\t    attavo build [N]\n8\t    attavo verify [N]\n9\t    attavo file-findings [N]\n10\t    attavo file-stops [N]\n11\t    attavo counsel [N]\n12\t    attavo record-only\n13\t    attavo attest [--partial] [N]\n14\t    attavo drive [N] [--until-ready] [--again] [--report]\n15\t    attavo drive --all\n16\t    attavo worker N <build|verify> NN\n17\t    attavo ledger [N] [--json]\n18\t    attavo stops [N] [--json]\n19\t    attavo test [N] [--all | <test>...] [--fresh]\n20\t\n21\tThe doctor is the definition of done. It asserts five proofs against a\n22\ttenant root and exits 1 until every proof holds:\n23\t\n24\t  1. every-gate-rejects      every gate in the manifest's [gates] table,\n25\t                             run against its rejection fixture, exits non-zero,\n26\t                             and carries a non-empty retires\n27\t  2. one-item-every-stage    one work item under paths.records carries a\n28\t                             record for every stage -- spec, approval,\n29\t                             build, verify -- all four introduced by one\n30\t                             merge commit reachable from HEAD\n31\t  3. no-commit-lacks-record  every commit on the default branch after the\n32\t                             manifest was introduced is named by a record's\n33\t                             sha or commits list, or itself writes under\n34\t                             paths.records (a record is committed with the\n35\t                             code it describes; an item's merge commit\n36\t                             carries its own record paths this way)\n37\t  4. no-stop-lacks-cause     every build or verify record under\n38\t                             paths.records at record_version 3 or later,\n39\t                             with a status other than pass, carries a stop\n40\t                             naming an enumerated class and provenance, a\n41\t                             non-empty detail when unclassed, the gates\n42\t                             heading when a build failed after running\n43\t                             them, and the tool's own error line when an\n44\t                             adapter exit ended the log -- records before\n45\t                             record_version 3 are counted and reported,\n46\t                             never refused\n47\t  5. every-attested-item-is-sealed\n48\t                             every merged item that carries a record for\n49\t                             every stage has a statement in the forge's\n50\t                             attestation store for its merge commit, read\n51\t                             through [forge].attestation_command -- a\n52\t                             merge at or before [forge].sealed_since is\n53\t                             named as before the window instead of failed.\n54\t                             [forge].attestation_command exiting 2 means\n55\t                             the store itself could not be read, reported\n56\t                             as not_read by item and never as unsealed\n57\t\n58\tNothing in doctor is a gate. The doctor reads; it never writes and it never\n59\tblocks a merge by itself. It is what CI runs to say whether the product\n60\tis done.\n61\t\n62\tspec-gate, approve, and approval-status are gates and writers. They run\n63\tfrom the tenant root (the current working directory); N, the work item id,\n64\tis read from the ATTAVO_ITEM environment variable when set, else from the\n65\tbranch (attavo/N-*). The doctor's first proof sets ATTAVO_ITEM for a\n66\trejection fixture's own item, so a gate's own command needs no argument\n67\teven while the enclosing repository sits on a real item's attavo/N-*\n68\tbranch. Every run of spec-gate or approve writes the next numbered attempt\n69\tfile under paths.records/N/ and never overwrites one already written. See\n70\tthe spec contract in the project's Phase 1 issue for the full rules each"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"f10e7365-697a-4187-94d0-b7fffbb7e98c","uuid":"177f74a3-4a64-4373-a4d3-cecd09a2c76c","timestamp":"2026-09-27T14:37:02.791Z","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/Users/davidbean/Projects/attavo-worktree-229/attavo/cli.py","content":"\"\"\"attavo: the command.\n\n    attavo doctor [TENANT_ROOT] [--json]\n    attavo spec-gate [N]\n    attavo approve [N] --by LOGIN\n    attavo approval-status [N]\n    attavo build [N]\n    attavo verify [N]\n    attavo file-findings [N]\n    attavo file-stops [N]\n    attavo counsel [N]\n    attavo record-only\n    attavo attest [--partial] [N]\n    attavo drive [N] [--until-ready] [--again] [--report]\n    attavo drive --all\n    attavo worker N <build|verify> NN\n    attavo ledger [N] [--json]\n    attavo stops [N] [--json]\n    attavo test [N] [--all | <test>...] [--fresh]\n\nThe doctor is the definition of done. It asserts five proofs against a\ntenant root and exits 1 until every proof holds:\n\n  1. every-gate-rejects      every gate in the manifest's [gates] table,\n                             run against its rejection fixture, exits non-zero,\n                             and carries a non-empty retires\n  2. one-item-every-stage    one work item under paths.records carries a\n                             record for every stage -- spec, approval,\n                             build, verify -- all four introduced by one\n                             merge commit reachable from HEAD\n  3. no-commit-lacks-record  every commit on the default branch after the\n                             manifest was introduced is named by a record's\n                             sha or commits list, or itself writes under\n                             paths.records (a record is committed with the\n                             code it describes; an item's merge commit\n                             carries its own record paths this way)\n  4. no-stop-lacks-cause     every build or verify record under\n                             paths.records at record_version 3 or later,\n                             with a status other than pass, carries a stop\n                             naming an enumerated class and provenance, a\n                             non-empty detail when unclassed, the gates\n                             heading when a build failed after running\n                             them, and the tool's own error line when an\n                             adapter exit ended the log -- records before\n                             record_version 3 are counted and reported,\n                             never refused\n  5. every-attested-item-is-sealed\n                             every merged item that carries a record for\n                             every stage has a statement in the forge's\n                             attestation store for its merge commit, read\n                             through [forge].attestation_command -- a\n                             merge at or before [forge].sealed_since is\n                             named as before the window instead of failed.\n                             [forge].attestation_command exiting 2 means\n                             the store itself could not be read, reported\n                             as not_read by item and never as unsealed\n\nNothing in doctor is a gate. The doctor reads; it never writes and it never\nblocks a merge by itself. It is what CI runs to say whether the product\nis done.\n\nspec-gate, approve, and approval-status are gates and writers. They run\nfrom the tenant root (the current working directory); N, the work item id,\nis read from the ATTAVO_ITEM environment variable when set, else from the\nbranch (attavo/N-*). The doctor's first proof sets ATTAVO_ITEM for a\nrejection fixture's own item, so a gate's own command needs no argument\neven while the enclosing repository sits on a real item's attavo/N-*\nbranch. Every run of spec-gate or approve writes the next numbered attempt\nfile under paths.records/N/ and never overwrites one already written. See\nthe spec contract in the project's Phase 1 issue for the full rules each","numLines":70,"startLine":1,"totalLines":395}}}
