{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_016nkMXTfRYFtjZtv145CxPD","type":"tool_result","content":"70\tthe spec contract in the project's Phase 1 issue for the full rules each\n71\tone enforces.\n72\t\n73\tbuild refuses (exit 1, naming the cause, no record) unless the manifest\n74\tdeclares [executor].build and [tests].select and [tests].run, and unless\n75\tapproval-status would print valid. It exports the executor's identity\n76\t(issue #33) into the adapter's environment as GIT_AUTHOR_NAME/EMAIL and\n77\tGIT_COMMITTER_NAME/EMAIL, set by the product and never the tenant's git\n78\tconfig, then invokes the named adapter (adapters/<name>/run) with the\n79\tspec, the corpus, and the branch. It refuses (status refused) a commit\n80\tbetween start_sha and HEAD not authored by that identity, checks that\n81\tevery path touched matches a spec claim, records the adapter's own\n82\tdeclared \"reports\" -- the fields adapters/<name>/conformance.json says\n83\tit can supply with a real value (issue #41), so a field it claims and\n84\tnever supplies is a defect the conformance suite catches rather than a\n85\tsilent null -- then runs the criteria, the\n86\ttests [tests].select and [tests].run name for the touched paths, and --\n87\twhen the manifest declares [checks].command -- the tenant's own\n88\twhole-tree check, from the tenant root. pass requires every criterion,\n89\tthe test run, and the tenant's checks (if declared) to exit 0; any\n90\tnon-zero exit iterates, with the failure as feedback, up to a fixed\n91\tbudget. [checks] is optional; a tenant that declares none is not\n92\trefused. Before the adapter is invoked it asks whether this machine can\n93\trun the checks -- of [checks].probe, run once inside [checks].probe_timeout_s\n94\t(exit 0 yes; anything else, or the bound, an environment refusal), or,\n95\tfor a tenant that declares no probe, by running [checks].command whole\n96\t(exit 2 no) -- and says both the question and the answer in the feed\n97\t(issue #212). The adapter is given ATTAVO_TEST_COMMAND, `attavo test N`,\n98\tand ATTAVO_TEST_TIMEOUT_S when [tests].call_timeout_s is declared; it\n99\tis not given the tenant's checks. It writes the next build-NN.json under paths.records/N/, with\n100\tthe adapter's transcript -- each iteration's gate output (criteria\n101\texits, the selected tests' stdout, the tenant's checks' tail) appended\n102\tunder an \"--- attavo gates, iteration N ---\" heading, issue #89 -- beside\n103\tit as build-NN.log. Every record whose status is not pass carries stop:\n104\t{class, provenance, detail}, derived from the refusal, halted, and log\n105\talready on hand (issue #89); a pass record carries stop: null. See the\n106\tbuild contract in the project's Phase 2 issue for the full rules it\n107\tenforces.\n108\t\n109\ttest [N] runs the tests [tests].select names for every path the item has\n110\tchanged since it left the default branch (refs/remotes/origin/HEAD),\n111\tcommitted or not and untracked included, paths.records aside, through\n112\t[tests].run (mode mapped, the default). test N <test>... runs exactly the\n113\tnamed tests instead (mode named), so an executor working on one test runs\n114\tone test; test N --all runs the whole suite through [tests].run with\n115\t\"tests\" as the one identifier (mode all), the same bound, event, and\n116\texclusion as the other two. Naming tests and --all together is refused\n117\t(exit 2). It prints how many were selected (or that none was, and runs\n118\tnothing), exits as the run does, and, when [tests].call_timeout_s is\n119\tdeclared and the run outlasts it, ends the run and everything it started\n120\tand exits 124. It exits 2 when it cannot name the changes or the selector\n121\tfails. A run that exits 0 is cached against a fingerprint of the tree\n122\t(HEAD, the diff against it, and every untracked unignored file's name and\n123\tcontent hash, together with the mode and the identifiers); asked again on\n124\tan unchanged tree it says so -- unchanged since the earlier run, not\n125\trerun -- without spending a second on it; --fresh reruns anyway. A\n126\tfailing run is never cached, since the next question after one is always\n127\twhether an edit fixed it. [tests].exclude_in_executor names test\n128\tidentifiers left out, and said so, when ATTAVO_STAGE is set (inside an\n129\texecutor); they run outside one and in CI. When ATTAVO_EVENTS is set, one\n130\tevent of kind test is written per invocation, naming the mode, the count\n131\tselected, the exit code, and the seconds spent (or that the answer came\n132\tfrom the cache). It is the one test command an executor is given (issue\n133\t#212); the product's own transport -- drive, worker, build, verify,\n134\tcounsel, file-stops -- refuses to run at all when ATTAVO_STAGE is set,\n135\tsince the transport is the pass's, not the executor's.\n136\t\n137\tverify refuses (exit 1) unless the item's latest build record has\n138\tstatus pass, and unless the manifest declares [forge].checks_command --\n139\ta tenant command, taking a full commit sha on argv, that prints one\n140\tline per check as \"<name> <conclusion>\". verify runs it on the build\n141\trecord's sha first: any conclusion other than success, neutral, or\n142\tskipped writes verify-NN.json with status returned and calls no\n143\tadapter, because a judge is never spent on a tree the forge already\n144\tcalled red. With the forge green, verify calls the adapter named by\n145\t[executor].verify (defaulting to [executor].build) with the diff since\n146\tthe build's approval, the spec, and the build record, and records its\n147\tfindings and its declared \"reports\" (issue #41). [executor.<adapter>.<stage>] shadows [executor.<adapter>] for\n148\tbuild or verify alone; both merge parent then stage before setting\n149\tATTAVO_ADAPTER_CONFIG, and the record's adapter_config is the merged\n150\tresult. Like build, every verify record whose status is not pass\n151\tcarries stop: {class, provenance, detail} (issue #89); a pass record\n152\tcarries stop: null. file-findings opens one tenant issue per finding in\n153\tthe item's latest verify record via [forge].file_issue_command, and\n154\trefuses (exit 1, nothing filed) a record carrying a finding with no\n155\tretires. See the verify contract in the project's Phase 2 issue for the\n156\tfull rules both enforce.\n157\t\n158\tfile-stops opens one tenant issue per stop record of the item with no\n159\tissue filed for it yet, through [forge].file_issue_command, naming the\n160\tclass, the provenance, the record path, and the log's last twenty\n161\tlines; a record it has already filed carries a <stage>-NN.filed marker\n162\tbeside it, holding the filing command's own stdout, so a second run\n163\tfiles nothing new. Like a build or verify record, this command writes\n164\tthe marker and leaves it uncommitted -- drive commits it, in the same\n165\tcommit as the record it names (issue #89). It refuses (exit 1,\n166\tnothing filed) a stop whose class is unclassed and whose detail is\n167\tempty -- a stop the product cannot even describe is not filed as if it\n168\tcould. See issue #89's lane for the full rules it enforces.\n169\t\n170\tcounsel reads the item's latest non-pass build or verify record -- or,\n171\twhen neither exists, its latest refused spec-gate record, the earliest\n172\tpoint a question can be answered inside the product, before any\n173\tapproval or executor spend (issue #133) -- and asks the tenant's\n174\t[executor].counsel adapter (defaulting to [executor].verify) a\n175\tread-only question about it: the record, its log, the spec (problem,\n176\tclaims, criteria, stub, including stub/.removed), paths.rulings, the\n177\titem's diff since approval, the tenant manifest, and this product's own\n178\troot (bin/attavo, adapters/, schema/, templates/) by path, under the\n179\tsame sandbox verify runs under. The adapter answers with class (the\n180\tstop enumeration, or unclassed), verdict (answer: a ruling text with\n181\tcitations; patch: a product defect's file, symbol, rejection test, and\n182\tdiff; person: a one-line question no rule covers), citations\n183\t(instruction, mechanism, guard, each a path and symbol or a ruling id),\n184\tand proposal (the ruling text, the patch, or the question). It writes\n185\tthe next counsel-NN.json under paths.records/N/, with the adapter's\n186\ttranscript beside it as counsel-NN.log, and commits nothing -- the\n187\tcaller commits, as with every stage. It refuses (exit 1, nothing\n188\twritten) when the item carries no non-pass build, verify, or spec-gate\n189\trecord to counsel. See issue #100's lane for the full rules it\n190\tenforces, and issue #133's for the spec-gate fallback.\n191\t\n192\trecord-only exits 0 when HEAD, against its first parent, touches only\n193\tpaths.records; 1 otherwise; 2 with no manifest. Core logic about a git\n194\tcheckout, not a forge's shell -- a workflow template's push-and-retrigger\n195\tguard is one line reading this exit code instead of carrying its own\n196\tcopy of the check.\n197\t\n198\tattest refuses (exit 1) unless the latest spec, approval, build, and\n199\tverify records for an item all exist and chain: the build's approval_sha\n200\tnames the latest approval, and the verify's build_sha names that build --\n201\ta re-approval after a build must force a re-run of what changed. With no\n202\tN given it derives the item from the record paths HEAD's merge commit\n203\ttouched under paths.records/<N>/, not from a branch name, which a squash\n204\tmerge discards and which names a forge's convention the product does not\n205\tknow; more than one item derived is a refusal naming what it found. Zero\n206\tis not a defect -- not every merge is an item merge -- exit 0, nothing\n207\tprinted but a line saying so.\n208\t\n209\tattest never writes. On a coherent chain it prints the attestation"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"f10e7365-697a-4187-94d0-b7