{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_016HnJdNetQ2qzVN4MLF3Kcd","type":"tool_result","content":"commit 15a774515f5aae7087031fe02c9b95297bb77ba3\nAuthor: attavo executor (claude-code) <executor+claude-code@attavo.invalid>\nDate:   Sun Sep 27 08:48:47 2026 -0600\n\n    attavo: an empty build is not a pass (item 229)\n    \n    The gate now reads the commit, never the executor's directory: criteria,\n    selected tests, and the tenant's checks run in a detached worktree of\n    HEAD (gate_checkout), so a path written and never committed cannot pass\n    on the executor's behalf. An iteration that ends with HEAD unchanged\n    since start_sha is fed back; the last such iteration halts the build\n    with the new stop class `empty` instead of passing or plain-failing.\n    Verify refuses a passing build record whose sha equals its start_sha,\n    and the doctor's seventh proof holds that no attested item's build is\n    empty, windowed by [doctor].built_since so item 227 (the specimen) is\n    named before the window rather than failing the tenant forever.\n    \n    Co-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n .github/workflows/ci.yml          |   1 +\n adapters/fixture/run              |  10 +++-\n attavo.toml                       |   5 +-\n attavo/build.py                   | 114 +++++++++++++++++++++++++++++---------\n attavo/cli.py                     |  32 +++++++++--\n attavo/doctor.py                  |  72 +++++++++++++++++++++++-\n attavo/stops.py                   |   2 +-\n attavo/verify.py                  |   4 ++\n schema/manifest.schema.json       |   5 ++\n schema/records/build.schema.json  |   4 +-\n schema/records/verify.schema.json |   4 +-\n tests/test_build.py               |  47 ++++++++++++++++\n tests/test_cli_help.py            |  10 ++++\n tests/test_doctor.py              |  66 ++++++++++++++++++++++\n tests/test_own_records_guard.py   |   2 +-\n tests/test_self_tenancy.py        |   6 +-\n tests/test_stub_ratio.py          |   2 +-\n tests/test_testtool.py            |  22 ++++----\n tests/test_verify.py              |  19 +++++++\n 19 files changed, 373 insertions(+), 54 deletions(-)","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"0ac05960-c509-42cc-ab1c-7aac0549dc0e","uuid":"157ec87d-178c-4fa6-9d1f-cb5fc46bbc15","timestamp":"2026-09-27T14:58:25.221Z","tool_use_result":{"stdout":"commit 15a774515f5aae7087031fe02c9b95297bb77ba3\nAuthor: attavo executor (claude-code) <executor+claude-code@attavo.invalid>\nDate:   Sun Sep 27 08:48:47 2026 -0600\n\n    attavo: an empty build is not a pass (item 229)\n    \n    The gate now reads the commit, never the executor's directory: criteria,\n    selected tests, and the tenant's checks run in a detached worktree of\n    HEAD (gate_checkout), so a path written and never committed cannot pass\n    on the executor's behalf. An iteration that ends with HEAD unchanged\n    since start_sha is fed back; the last such iteration halts the build\n    with the new stop class `empty` instead of passing or plain-failing.\n    Verify refuses a passing build record whose sha equals its start_sha,\n    and the doctor's seventh proof holds that no attested item's build is\n    empty, windowed by [doctor].built_since so item 227 (the specimen) is\n    named before the window rather than failing the tenant forever.\n    \n    Co-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n .github/workflows/ci.yml          |   1 +\n adapters/fixture/run              |  10 +++-\n attavo.toml                       |   5 +-\n attavo/build.py                   | 114 +++++++++++++++++++++++++++++---------\n attavo/cli.py                     |  32 +++++++++--\n attavo/doctor.py                  |  72 +++++++++++++++++++++++-\n attavo/stops.py                   |   2 +-\n attavo/verify.py                  |   4 ++\n schema/manifest.schema.json       |   5 ++\n schema/records/build.schema.json  |   4 +-\n schema/records/verify.schema.